course: dictionary
lesson: 15407
title: Spotting: seeing and noticing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Spotting means noticing or seeing something, often something that is hard to find. «Mum spotted her keys under the newspaper.» The keys were hidden, but Mum noticed them anyway.
explain: You can spot patterns, mistakes and clues too. «Can you spot the pattern in 2, 4, 6, 8?» Each number goes up by 2. Good readers and mathematicians are good at spotting these things.
explain: Spotting can also be a hobby. «Ravi goes bird spotting every Sunday with his grandad.» Bird spotting means watching for birds and noting the ones you see. In gym, spotting means standing by to catch someone so they stay safe.
fact: Spotting is a verb (spot, spots, spotted, spotting) and can also be a noun, as in «bird spotting».
fact: «Spotting» means noticing or seeing something, often something hard to find.
fact: «Spotting» can mean a hobby of watching for and recording things, like «train spotting».
fact: In sports and gym, «spotting» means standing by to help and catch someone so they do not get hurt.
fact: A detective is good at spotting clues, and you can practise spotting patterns in maths.
exercise: «Mum was quick at spotting the missing sock under the sofa.» What does spotting mean here? | *Noticing or seeing something | Washing clothes | Making a loud noise | Throwing something away
exercise: Ravi goes bird spotting every Sunday. What is bird spotting? | A sport where you catch balls | Cleaning out a bird cage | *A hobby of watching for and recording birds | A type of bird food
exercise: In gym, Mia stands behind the child on the bars to help if they fall. What is Mia doing? | Shouting at the children | Sleeping on the mat | Looking for a lost bag | *Spotting, standing by to catch them
test: Ella is ___ the differences between the two pictures. Which word fits best? | *spotting | spot | spots | spotted
test: «Can you spot the mistake in this sum?» What does spot mean here? | Draw a dot | Hide | *Notice or find | Erase
exam: Which sentence uses spotting to mean noticing something? | *The detective was good at spotting the clue. | The shop sells spotting cards for children. | She ate the spotting for lunch.
